#: inc/security.php:1045
msgid "Spam tools publish from outside the site with a stored password. These switches close the doors they use. Writing in the editor is not affected, and visitors see no change."
msgstr ""

#: inc/security.php:1047
msgid "Turn off XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#: inc/security.php:1047
msgid "xmlrpc.php answers 403 and the pingback header goes. On Apache the theme also blocks it in .htaccess, and removes that block when this is switched off. The Jetpack plugin and old mobile apps need XML-RPC."
msgstr ""

#: inc/security.php:1050
msgid "The web server also refuses xmlrpc.php: the theme keeps a \"Block xmlrpc.php\" section in .htaccess and repairs it if it goes missing."
msgstr ""

#: inc/security.php:1052
msgid "The theme could not write .htaccess (the server is not Apache, or the file is read-only). WordPress still refuses xmlrpc.php; ask the host to deny it at the server as well."
msgstr ""

#: inc/security.php:1054
msgid "Turn off application passwords"
msgstr ""

#: inc/security.php:1054
msgid "Stored application passwords stop working at once. Revoke them as well, below, so they cannot return if this is switched off."
msgstr ""

#: inc/security.php:1055
msgid "Allow REST API changes only from a logged-in browser"
msgstr ""

#: inc/security.php:1055
msgid "Any request that creates, changes or deletes content while logged in must come from a browser session on this site. Basic authentication and passwords sent in a header are refused. Reading through the API, and anything visitors send without logging in, is unchanged."
msgstr ""

