msgstr ""

#: inc/settings.php:1144
msgid "Setup runs by itself on the first admin visit after the theme is activated or updated; this button runs it again. It creates any missing guide pages in both languages, places the Malay pages beneath the Malay home at /ms/, pairs each page with its translation and sets the front page. Every page whose article ships with the theme is filled and published; pages with no article (About and Contact) stay drafts. When the theme ships a new version of an article, a page nobody has edited takes it (WordPress keeps the old text as a revision); a page an editor has changed is never overwritten and is listed under \"Edited, not updated\". Obsolete copies of guide pages left by earlier setups go to the trash; pages the theme did not create are never touched. Featured images an editor chose are kept. Empty title tags and meta descriptions are filled from the keyword plan."
msgstr ""

